IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part2a-termination`

-- Tests for ea1-part2a-termination.l4 (ss 8 to 17).  Every expected value is written
-- from the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run;
-- the reading of each case is in the comment beside it.  Nothing is copied from the
-- encoding's own output.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 8 Illegal terms of contract of service`
-- A term of a contract of service that provides a condition of service less favourable
-- than one the Act prescribes is illegal and void.
#ASSERT `s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A condition that is not less favourable: the section does not say it is valid.
#ASSERT `s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A term that is not a term of a contract of service is outside the section.
#ASSERT `s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A term that provides no condition of service is outside the section.
#ASSERT `s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 9 Termination of contract`
-- (1): arguments are: for a specified piece of work, completed, for a specified period, expired, otherwise terminated.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The work is not yet completed and no period has expired: "terminates when" counts as "where", so the answer is no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The period has not yet expired: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless otherwise terminated in accordance with the provisions of this Part": already terminated otherwise, the subsection does not terminate it.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments are: for an unspecified period, terminated by either party in accordance with this Part.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the contract of service is deemed to run` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the contract of service is deemed to run` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A contract for a specified period is not one that subsection (2) speaks of.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the contract of service is deemed to run` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 10 Notice of termination of contract`
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the party may at any time give the other party notice of intention to terminate the contract of service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the party may at any time give the other party notice of intention to terminate the contract of service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): the contract's provision governs (reading A); where there is none, subsection (3).
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the length of the notice, in days` (JUST 14) (JUST 7) EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the length of the notice, in days` (JUST 3) (JUST 7) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the length of the notice, in days` NOTHING (JUST 7) EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the length of the notice, in days` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the length of the notice is the same for both employer and employee` 14 14
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10(2) the length of the notice is the same for both employer and employee` 14 7)

-- (3): the employment began on 1 January 2024 (a leap year: 182 days make 26 weeks on 1 July 2024).
`began 1 January 2024` MEANS `Dates of the employment` WITH `began on` IS Date 1 1 2024, `ended on` IS NOTHING
-- (a) less than 26 weeks: 181 days elapsed on 30 June 2024; one day's notice.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 30 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST 1
-- (b) 26 weeks or more but less than 2 years: 182 days elapsed on 1 July 2024; one week's notice.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 1 7 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST 7
-- (c) 2 years or more but less than 5 years: 2 years are up on 1 January 2026; 2 weeks' notice.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 31 12 2028) TRUE EQUALS JUST 14
-- (d) 5 years or more: 5 years are up on 1 January 2029; 4 weeks' notice.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 1 1 2029) TRUE EQUALS JUST 28
-- The notice day itself is the day of beginning: no days elapsed, one day's notice.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 1 1 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST 1
-- A person not employed under a contract of service is not one the subsection speaks of.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 1 7 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice dated before the employment began is outside the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` `began 1 January 2024` (Date 31 12 2023) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8 applied to the notice term: a 3-day term against the 7-day least notice is void as to 4 days, if the shorter notice is less favourable to the employee.
#ASSERT `s 8 the number of days by which the contract's term on the length of notice is void as shorter than section 10(3)` 3 (JUST 7) TRUE EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `s 8 the number of days by which the contract's term on the length of notice is void as shorter than section 10(3)` 7 (JUST 7) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8 the number of days by which the contract's term on the length of notice is void as shorter than section 10(3)` 3 (JUST 7) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8 the number of days by which the contract's term on the length of notice is void as shorter than section 10(3)` 3 NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4)
#ASSERT `s 10(4) the party may waive the party's right to notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(4) the party may waive the party's right to notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5)
`a written notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH `given by` IS `Party who is the employee`, `given on` IS Date 1 3 2026, `last day of the notice` IS Date 7 3 2026, `in writing` IS TRUE
`an oral notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH `given by` IS `Party who is the employer`, `given on` IS Date 1 3 2026, `last day of the notice` IS Date 7 3 2026, `in writing` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the notice is written` `a written notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "The notice must be written": an oral notice does not meet it.
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the notice is written` `an oral notice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the notice may be given on the day` (Date 25 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "the day on which the notice is given is included": 7 days from 1 March are 1 to 7 March.
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the last day of the period of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST (Date 7 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the last day of the period of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2026)
-- the end of the month rolls over: 28 days from 20 February 2026 end on 19 March.
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the last day of the period of the notice` (Date 20 2 2026) 28 EQUALS JUST (Date 19 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the last day of the period of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 11 Termination of contract without notice`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice, or without waiting for the notice to expire` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice, or without waiting for the notice to expire` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "less than a month": a period starting 1 March 2026 is a month at 31 days (it ends on 31 March).
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 1 3 2026) 30
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 1 3 2026) 31)
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 1 2 2026) 27
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 1 2 2026) 28)
-- A notice on the 31st: the next month has no 31st, so the month ends on its last day (fork F-11(1)).
-- 31 January 2026 with 28 days (31 Jan to 27 Feb) is less than a month; 29 days (31 Jan to 28 Feb) is a month.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 31 1 2026) 28
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` (Date 31 1 2026) 29)
-- monthly-rated, notice of 5 days: 5 days at the gross rate for one day's work (here 100): 500.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` NOTHING TRUE TRUE 5 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 500
-- monthly-rated, the day rate is not known (seam S6 gave none): no answer.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` NOTHING TRUE TRUE 5 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not monthly-rated: the salary at the gross rate that would have accrued, as stated (700).
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` (JUST 700) FALSE TRUE 7 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 700
-- monthly-rated but the notice is a month or more: the salary that would have accrued, as stated (3000).
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` (JUST 3000) TRUE FALSE 31 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` NOTHING FALSE FALSE 31 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No wilful breach: "in the event of" read as "where" (assumed, fork F-EVENT): the answer is no.
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 12 Contractual age`
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the person is competent to enter into a contract of service` 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the person is competent to enter into a contract of service` 18 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): below 18 and not for the person's benefit: not enforceable, nothing recoverable.
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the contract of service as an employee is enforceable against the person` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the contract of service as an employee is enforceable against the person` 17 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the contract of service as an employee is enforceable against the person` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) damages or indemnity are recoverable from the person in respect of the contract of service` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) damages or indemnity are recoverable from the person in respect of the contract of service` 17 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) damages or indemnity are recoverable from the person in respect of the contract of service` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 13 When contract deemed to be broken by employer and employee`
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the employer is deemed to have broken the employer's contract of service with the employee` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the employer is deemed to have broken the employer's contract of service with the employee` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments are: days continuously absent, prior leave, reasonable excuse, informs or attempts to inform.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (b): has an excuse but neither informs nor tries to.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` 3 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an excuse and informs: neither limb.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "more than 2 days": exactly 2 is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 14 Dismissal`
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the employer may dismiss the employee without notice` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the employer may dismiss the employee without notice` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the employer may dismiss the employee without notice` `Ground: some other ground or none` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the employer may instantly down-grade the employee instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the employer may instantly down-grade the employee instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: some other ground or none` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): suspension without pay for not more than one week (7 days).
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the employer may instantly suspend the employee from work without payment of salary instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An eighth day is outside the period the text fixes in its own words ("not exceeding one week"): no (ruled 2026-11-05 (a)).
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the employer may instantly suspend the employee from work without payment of salary instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` TRUE 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the employer may instantly suspend the employee from work without payment of salary instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: some other ground or none` TRUE 3 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): arguments are: dismissal, relevant employee, considers dismissed without just cause or excuse, s 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open, relief.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a sum the Commissioner considers just is not one of "either of the following remedies".
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: payment of a sum the Commissioner considers just` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a relevant employee (JUST FALSE): the grant is "where a relevant employee considers": outside it.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the employee does not consider that he or she was dismissed without just cause.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the borrowed answers pass a NOTHING on.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING `Relief: compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2A): arguments are: managerial or executive, manner of dismissal, complete months served.
-- limb (a): managerial, dismissed with notice, 6 months' service (at least 6).
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` TRUE `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (a) not met at 5 months, and no other limb applies to a managerial employee dismissed with notice: the definition "means", so no.
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` TRUE `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- limb (a)(ii): without notice but with salary in lieu.
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` TRUE `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice but with payment of any salary in lieu of notice` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` TRUE `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice but with payment of any salary in lieu of notice` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- limb (b): without notice and without salary in lieu: any length of service.
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` TRUE `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (c): an employee not employed in a managerial or an executive position.
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` FALSE `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` FALSE `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (3): arguments are: the body is the Tribunal, satisfied, relief.
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `Relief: compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Tribunal is not satisfied: an unmet "if", so the answer is no.
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` NOTHING TRUE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay compensation, an amount of wages determined by the Tribunal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay compensation, an amount of wages determined by the Tribunal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The body is not a Tribunal: "If a Tribunal hearing the claim" is unmet, so the answer is no.
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay compensation, an amount of wages determined by the Tribunal` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (8)(a): suspension for an inquiry: up to one week, or a longer period the Commissioner has determined.
#ASSERT `s 14(8)(a) the employer may suspend the employee from work for the period` 7 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Eight days with no longer period determined: outside the periods the text fixes (ruled 2026-11-05 (a)).
#ASSERT `s 14(8)(a) the employer may suspend the employee from work for the period` 8 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(8)(a) the employer may suspend the employee from work for the period` 10 (JUST 14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(8)(a) the employer may suspend the employee from work for the period` 15 (JUST 14) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8)(b): at least half the salary during the suspension (a salary of 1000 for the period: 500).
#ASSERT `s 14(8)(b) the least the employer must pay the employee during the suspension` 1000 EQUALS 500
-- (9)
#ASSERT `s 14(9) the employer must immediately restore the full amount of the salary withheld` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(9) the employer must immediately restore the full amount of the salary withheld` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(9) the amount the employer must restore` FALSE 800 EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 14(9) the amount the employer must restore` TRUE 800 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The regulative rule: the employer who restores at once fulfils; one who does not, breaches (read the two traces).
#TRACE `s 14(9) the employer's duty to restore the salary` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 14(9) the employer` DOES `s 14(9) restore to the employee the full amount of the salary withheld` AT 0
#TRACE `s 14(9) the employer's duty to restore the salary` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 14(9) the employer` DOES `s 14(9) restore to the employee the full amount of the salary withheld` AT 3

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 15 Termination by employee threatened by danger`
-- arguments are: the employee is the person threatened, the person threatened is a dependant, immediate, to the person by violence or disease, undertook to run it.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a dependant is threatened.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person who is not a dependant (the definition says no), for example a cousin: "where the employee or the employee’s dependant is immediately threatened" is unmet (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the definition of dependant gives no answer: no answer.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the employee undertook to run the danger by the contract of service.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the danger is not immediate / not by violence or disease.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 16 Liability on breach of contract`
#ASSERT `s 16 the party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay the other party the sum` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 16 the party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay the other party the sum` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a party who did not break the contract is outside the section.
#ASSERT `s 16 the party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay the other party the sum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the sum is the section 11 sum where there was no notice; with insufficient notice the Act does not say.
#ASSERT `s 16 the sum the party is liable to pay` TRUE (JUST 500) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 16 the sum the party is liable to pay` FALSE (JUST 500) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16 the sum the party is liable to pay` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 17 Contract of service not to restrict rights of employees to join, participate in or organise trade unions`
#ASSERT `s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` `s 17(a) the right to join a registered trade union` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` `s 17(b) the right to participate in the activities of a registered trade union, whether as an officer of the trade union or otherwise` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` `s 17(c) the right to associate with any other persons for the purpose of organising a trade union in accordance with the provisions of the Trade Unions Act 1940` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Subject to any other written law": another written law restricts the right.
#ASSERT `s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` `s 17(a) the right to join a registered trade union` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a right the section does not name.
#ASSERT `s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` `s 17 a right that the section does not name` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05 (periods, "where" and scope limits): expected
-- values written from the text of ss 9, 12(2), 14 and 15.
-- s 9(1): the subsection speaks only of a contract for a specified piece of work or a specified period; a contract for neither: scope limit (c), not covered.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(2): the bar on enforcement and on damages, a person aged 17.
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on enforcing the contract of service as an employee against the person applies` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on enforcing the contract of service as an employee against the person applies` 17 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on enforcing the contract of service as an employee against the person applies` 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on recovering damages or indemnity from the person in respect of the contract of service applies` 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on recovering damages or indemnity from the person in respect of the contract of service applies` 17 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the bar on recovering damages or indemnity from the person in respect of the contract of service applies` 25 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1)(b): without a due inquiry the permission "instead of dismissing" does not arise: scope limit, not covered.
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the employer may instantly suspend the employee from work without payment of salary instead of dismissing the employee` `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service` FALSE 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(2): no dismissal at all, so "where a relevant employee considers that he or she has been dismissed" is unmet (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(2): "subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016", which the caller says does not leave the claim open: the text of that Act is not among the sources, not covered.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) `Relief: compensation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(3)(a): the body is not a Tribunal; and a body not known to be one with the Tribunal not satisfied: the first is an unmet "if", the second is not known.
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` NOTHING TRUE `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15: a danger that is not immediate defeats the "where" whatever the dependant question gives.
#ASSERT `s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
